    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44297" root="&#xA;                        هزم&#xA;                    " body-key="h1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَزْمَةٌ</span></b> 
                         The [<i>purring,</i> or] <i>sound of the throat</i>
of a cat. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  The <i>pit between the two
collar-bones.</i> (TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ترب</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [The <i>pit</i>
above a horse's eye.] (K, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقْبٌ</span>.) See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُنْعُبَةٌ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَلْتَةٌ</span>: and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُقْمٌ</span>, where it seems
to mean <i>a stricture:</i> it generally and properly
signifies <i>a depression,</i> or <i>dint:</i> or <i>a pit,</i> or <i>small
hollow, resembling a dint:</i> see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيْبٌ</span>.

